  <p>Vocele's plans cost $14.99, $29.99 or $49.99 a month. Every plan meters spoken conversation and pronunciation scoring by the month: Core includes 150 minutes of talk and 30 of pronunciation scoring, and the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> lists the rest.</p>

  <h2>Which one should you pick</h2>

  <p><strong>BoldVoice</strong> is the better choice if your English is already strong and an American accent is the goal, if you learn best from a coach on video, or if you practice on Android.</p>

  <p>Pick <strong>Vocele</strong> if your sounds are fine in drills and slip in conversation, if you want grammar fixes and saved words in the same place as your accent work, or if you're learning a language other than English.</p>

  <p>Still comparing pronunciation specialists? <a href="/vs/elsa">Vocele vs ELSA Speak</a> covers the other big one. If the real choice is an app or a private accent coach, I price Vocele against tutoring at $200 to $320 a month, and <a href="/blog/ai-speaking-coach-vs-human-tutor">the AI coach vs human tutor comparison</a> is honest about where apps lose.</p>

  <p>Vocele isn't on the App Store yet. If you want your accent trained inside real conversation, <a href="/pricing">see the plans and the 3-day trial</a>. I'll update this page when the listing goes live.</p>
